@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `ind-a-tests-fixtures`
IMPORT `g2-validity`
IMPORT `g2-second-schedule`
IMPORT `g2-conditions`

-- ind-a-tests-sch2.l4: independent tests by ind-a for s.6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, one scenario per row
-- or more.  Every number was read from the gazette (Sefer HaChukim 3349 pp. 201-205), not from the wiki.
-- Expected values decided before the encoding was opened (work/ind-a/expectations.md, SCH2-*).
-- Stated assumptions for every grant question: adult Israeli citizen and resident, clean record, the
-- programme had the Registrar's consent (s.19(b)), no foreign qualification, the fee was paid.

§ `ind-a Second Schedule helpers`

GIVEN requirement IS A `Requirement of the Second Schedule`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ind-a ceiling of` requirement MEANS
    CONSIDER requirement
    WHEN `training of up to` ceiling certificate THEN ceiling
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN item IS A `Second Schedule item`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`ind-a ceilings of item` item MEANS
    map `ind-a ceiling of` (item's `column B: any one of`)

GIVEN application IS AN Application
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`ind-a items that apply` application MEANS
    map (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number`) (`training required for the licence sought` application `ind-a commencement day`)

GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `training done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a must grant` application `training done` MEANS
    `the Registrar must grant the licence` application `ind-a commencement day` FALSE `training done` TRUE FALSE TRUE

GIVEN certificates IS A LIST OF Certificate
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
GIVETH AN Application
`ind-a holder of` certificates `seeking` kind MEANS
    `ind-a application` (`ind-a applicant holding` certificates) kind (YMD 2026 3 1)

GIVEN licences IS A LIST OF Licence
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
GIVETH AN Application
`ind-a licensee holding` licences `seeking` kind MEANS
    `ind-a application` (`ind-a applicant in full` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a record` FALSE FALSE) licences EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE) kind (YMD 2026 3 1)

GIVEN technician IS A BOOLEAN
      `practical engineer` IS A BOOLEAN
      programme IS A BOOLEAN
      engineer IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
GIVETH AN Application
`ind-a registered applicant` technician `practical engineer` programme engineer kind MEANS
    `ind-a application` (`ind-a applicant in full` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a record` FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY technician `practical engineer` programme engineer EMPTY FALSE FALSE) kind (YMD 2026 3 1)

GIVEN periods IS A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH AN Application
`ind-a worker with` periods `seeking` kind `on` day MEANS
    `ind-a application` (`ind-a applicant in full` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a record` FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE periods FALSE FALSE) kind day

-- A grade 1 licence granted 2024-06-01 (in force until 2029-03-31), and a grade 2 licence likewise.
`ind-a grade 1 licence held` MEANS LIST `ind-a plain licence` (YMD 2024 6 1) `grade 1 licence`
`ind-a grade 2 licence held` MEANS LIST `ind-a plain licence` (YMD 2024 6 1) `grade 2 licence`

-- Twelve months of work in the three years before an application of 2026-01-01.
`ind-a one year in the last three` MEANS LIST `ind-a worked` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31)
-- Eleven months in the last three years, and three years earlier inside the last seven.
`ind-a three years in the last seven` MEANS LIST `ind-a worked` (YMD 2019 1 1) (YMD 2021 12 31), `ind-a worked` (YMD 2025 2 1) (YMD 2025 12 31)
-- Eleven months in the last three years, and only eighteen months more inside the last seven.
`ind-a too little experience` MEANS LIST `ind-a worked` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2022 6 30), `ind-a worked` (YMD 2025 2 1) (YMD 2025 12 31)
-- Twelve months of work before an application in July 2028.
`ind-a one year before July 2028` MEANS LIST `ind-a worked` (YMD 2027 7 1) (YMD 2028 7 1)

§ `The numbers of column B, read from the gazette`

#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part A, item 1` EQUALS LIST 350, 0
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part A, item 2` EQUALS LIST 220
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part A, item 3` EQUALS LIST 50
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part B, item 1` EQUALS LIST 480, 0
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part B, item 2` EQUALS LIST 0
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part B, item 3` EQUALS LIST 100
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part B, item 4` EQUALS LIST 330
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part B, item 5` EQUALS LIST 50
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part B, item 6` EQUALS LIST 50
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part C, item 1` EQUALS LIST 720
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part C, item 2` EQUALS LIST 0
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part C, item 3` EQUALS LIST 290
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part C, item 4` EQUALS LIST 240
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part C, item 5` EQUALS LIST 455
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part C, item 6` EQUALS LIST 200
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part C, item 7` EQUALS LIST 50
#ASSERT `ind-a ceilings of item` `Second Schedule, Part C, item 8` EQUALS LIST 230
-- Column C: only the experience rows carry the three-year note.
#ASSERT `Second Schedule, Part A, item 2`'s `column C: valid for three years from the commencement day`
#ASSERT `Second Schedule, Part B, item 4`'s `column C: valid for three years from the commencement day`
#ASSERT `Second Schedule, Part C, item 5`'s `column C: valid for three years from the commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Second Schedule, Part C, item 4`'s `column C: valid for three years from the commencement day`
-- C-08: the note's last day is 2028-07-16 (three years after 2025-07-16, IL s.10(b), no IL s.10(c)).
#ASSERT `Second Schedule column C — the last day of the three years beginning on` `ind-a commencement day` EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `Second Schedule column C — the experience items are in force on the day` `ind-a commencement day` (YMD 2028 7 16)
#ASSERT NOT `Second Schedule column C — the experience items are in force on the day` `ind-a commencement day` (YMD 2028 7 17)

§ `Part A: grade 1`

-- SCH2-A1b: Ministry of Education 3 study units suffices with nothing more.
#ASSERT `ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`) `seeking` `grade 1 licence`) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`) `seeking` `grade 1 licence`) FALSE
-- SCH2-A2a: twelve months in the last three years: row 2 (training of up to 220 hours) applies.
#ASSERT elem 2 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a one year in the last three` `seeking` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)))
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a one year in the last three` `seeking` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a one year in the last three` `seeking` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)) FALSE
-- SCH2-A2b: limb (2), three years within seven.
#ASSERT elem 2 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a three years in the last seven` `seeking` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)))
-- SCH2-A2c: neither limb.
#ASSERT NOT elem 2 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a too little experience` `seeking` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)))
-- SCH2-A2d, A2e: the three-year note, tested on the application day.
#ASSERT elem 2 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a one year before July 2028` `seeking` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 7 16)))
#ASSERT NOT elem 2 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a one year before July 2028` `seeking` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17)))
-- SCH2-A3a, A3b: an ungraded Division certificate needs up to 50 hours more.
#ASSERT `ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated`) `seeking` `grade 1 licence`) EQUALS LIST 3
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated`) `seeking` `grade 1 licence`) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated`) `seeking` `grade 1 licence`) FALSE
-- SCH2-A-gap (literal reading): 5 study units are not listed in Part A; without the course, not met.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units`) `seeking` `grade 1 licence`) FALSE

§ `Part B: grade 2`

-- SCH2-B2a, B2b
#ASSERT `ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a registered applicant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `grade 2 licence`) EQUALS LIST 2
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a registered applicant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `grade 2 licence`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a registered applicant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `grade 2 licence`) FALSE
-- SCH2-B3a..d
#ASSERT elem 3 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a licensee holding` `ind-a grade 1 licence held` `seeking` `grade 2 licence`))
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a licensee holding` `ind-a grade 1 licence held` `seeking` `grade 2 licence`) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a licensee holding` `ind-a grade 1 licence held` `seeking` `grade 2 licence`) FALSE
#ASSERT elem 3 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`) `seeking` `grade 2 licence`))
#ASSERT elem 3 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`) `seeking` `grade 2 licence`))
-- SCH2-B4a, B4b
#ASSERT elem 4 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a one year in the last three` `seeking` `grade 2 licence` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)))
#ASSERT NOT elem 4 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a one year before July 2028` `seeking` `grade 2 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17)))
-- SCH2-B5a..c
#ASSERT elem 5 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated`) `seeking` `grade 2 licence`))
#ASSERT elem 5 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a certificate of the Training Division vocational school for youth`) `seeking` `grade 2 licence`))
#ASSERT elem 5 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units`) `seeking` `grade 2 licence`))
-- SCH2-B6a
#ASSERT `ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a registered applicant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `grade 2 licence`) EQUALS LIST 6
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a registered applicant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `grade 2 licence`) TRUE
-- SCH2-B-gap (literal reading): a practical engineer has no Part B row of his own; without the course, not met.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a registered applicant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `grade 2 licence`) FALSE

§ `Part C: grade 3`

-- SCH2-C2a, C2b
#ASSERT `ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a registered applicant` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `grade 3 licence`) EQUALS LIST 2
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a registered applicant` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `grade 3 licence`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a registered applicant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `grade 3 licence`) FALSE
-- SCH2-C3a
#ASSERT elem 3 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a licensee holding` `ind-a grade 1 licence held` `seeking` `grade 3 licence`))
#ASSERT elem 3 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`) `seeking` `grade 3 licence`))
#ASSERT elem 3 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`) `seeking` `grade 3 licence`))
-- SCH2-C4a, C4b (the gazette puts the 240 hours in column B)
#ASSERT elem 4 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a licensee holding` `ind-a grade 2 licence held` `seeking` `grade 3 licence`))
#ASSERT elem 4 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`) `seeking` `grade 3 licence`))
#ASSERT elem 4 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units`) `seeking` `grade 3 licence`))
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a licensee holding` `ind-a grade 2 licence held` `seeking` `grade 3 licence`) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a licensee holding` `ind-a grade 2 licence held` `seeking` `grade 3 licence`) FALSE
-- SCH2-C5a, C5b
#ASSERT elem 5 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a one year in the last three` `seeking` `grade 3 licence` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)))
#ASSERT NOT elem 5 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a worker with` `ind-a one year before July 2028` `seeking` `grade 3 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17)))
-- SCH2-C6
#ASSERT elem 6 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated`) `seeking` `grade 3 licence`))
-- SCH2-C7a
#ASSERT `ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a registered applicant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `grade 3 licence`) EQUALS LIST 7
-- SCH2-C8a, C8b
#ASSERT `ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a registered applicant` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `grade 3 licence`) EQUALS LIST 8
#ASSERT NOT elem 8 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a registered applicant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `grade 3 licence`))
